+## Preserve the critical register while improving readability
+
+Author's direction, 24 September 2026: carry the concrete, poetic, technical and critical encounter approach through the remaining sequences, consulting their other markdown drafts. Start where the current text and content are furthest from that approach, rather than applying equal revision pressure or merely continuing a mechanical queue.
+
+A sequence may deliberately investigate a different critical problem. Recover that problem from intent, critical, technical, tutorial and other drafts before changing its voice. A forensic or failed-affordance encounter may belong; improve how a reader reaches and understands it rather than turning every absence into a repair or erasing every failure from the book.
+
+Look for queer possibilities in the particular relations the work permits: desire, accommodation, support, withdrawal, attachment, ambiguity, different uses of the same form. Do not equate queerness with noise, disorder, maximum complexity or a compulsory final sentence about exclusion. Readability should make the particular question more available, not homogenise it.
+
+Source findings guide the writing and artifact decisions. Move implementation bookkeeping out of the reading when it no longer advances the encounter, preserving it as dated supporting material. Keep the distinctions a reader needs to understand what they see or can do. If the necessary encounter is missing, recover or build it within the task's ownership, or ask one specific artistic question while continuing independent work.
